<title>BRAZIL: Strike threat still looms in Brazil's Santos port.</title>
<headline>Strike threat still looms in Brazil's Santos port.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stevedores at the key Brazilian port of Santos continued to occupy two vessels at the private terminal of steel company Companhia Siderurgica Paulista (Cosipa) and port authorities said a fresh strike could erupt at any time.</p>
<p>The rest of the port was operating normally although light rains were interrupting the normal loading of grains, which continued intermittently through the morning as the weather allowed.</p>
</text>
